<title>CHINA: PEREGRINE BUYS EMERGING MARKETS BUSINESS.</title>
<headline>PEREGRINE BUYS EMERGING MARKETS BUSINESS.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peregrine Investments Holdings Ltd said it had agreed to buy the emerging markets business of Sweden's investment banking group Carnegie AB.</p>
<p>Carnegie Emerging Markets has a team of 26 and produces research on companies in Poland, Turkey, Israel and Greece.</p>
<p>It is also active in Egypt, Hungary, Morocco, Romania and the Czech Republic and in time, Peregrine said it would look to expand the franchise by including Kazakhstan and Russia.</p>
<p>&quot;These markets are at a stage where emerging Asia was 10 years ago. The growth potential is huge,&quot; Peregrine Securities International chief executive officer Andrew Jamieson said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong News Room (852) 2843 6345</p>
</text>
